## Context

Ticket 0710 (PR #385) fixed the toolbar tooltip's false scope: the sitter
covers every Zotero library (its census is unscoped SQL over
`itemAttachments`), but the coverage percentage read as if it applied to
"the library" singular. 0710's own review found the identical false scope
survives on three other surfaces it deliberately did not touch (out of
scope for that ticket -- named as a follow-up rather than fixed silently):

- The dialog heading, `bootstrap.js:325` (approximate line, may have moved).
- That heading's associated coverage figure, `bootstrap.js:254`.
- The launch/confirmation prompt, `bootstrap.js:582`, whose exact wording
  ("Indexer toute la bibliotheque") is pinned by `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py:446`
  -- changing it needs that test updated too.

`describeSDTScope()` (added by 0710) is already a reusable, tested composer
for exactly this -- library name enumeration (one, up to three, then a
count), minus feeds. This ticket is mostly wiring it into three more call
sites, not new design.

## Work

- Read the current line numbers for all three surfaces (they will have
  drifted since 0710 filed this).
- Wire `describeSDTScope()` into the dialog heading and its coverage figure.
- Update the launch prompt's wording to include scope, and update
  `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py:446`'s pinned string to match.
- Reuse the same 10Hz-render performance consideration 0710's own review
  raised (`describeSDTScope()` re-enumerates every library on every render
  tick) -- if this ticket adds more call sites to the same hot path, that
  memoization concern becomes more pressing; consider whether to address it
  here or file it separately if it's not already tracked.

## Acceptance

- [x] Dialog heading and its coverage figure state the library scope,
      consistent with the toolbar tooltip's wording (0710/0691's vocabulary)
      — with one qualification, disclosed rather than silently met. The
      HEADING carries the scope textually: `renderState` recomposes the
      overall-progress `<legend>` on every tick as
      `[sdtText('section-global'), describeSDTScope()]`
      (`bootstrap.js:1097-1099`), through the same composer the tooltip uses,
      so a lazily-loaded group library cannot leave it naming a stale set.
      The coverage FIGURE is scoped structurally rather than textually: it is
      `sdt-status`, a child of the very fieldset that legend heads
      (`bootstrap.js:1228-1230`), and the progress bar beside it is bound to
      that legend by `aria-labelledby` (`:1220`). Repeating the enumeration on
      the figure's own line was reviewed and not taken — it would restate the
      scope twice within one bordered group, on a line re-rendered at 10 Hz.
      The reasoning is recorded in the code at `bootstrap.js:1084-1090`, so a
      later reader meets it as a decision.
- [x] Launch prompt states scope; its pinned test string updated to match —
      `bootstrap.js:1637` composes `launch-question` with
      `describeSDTScope()`; the pinned string is now "Index every library
      tonight?" (`bootstrap.js:251`), asserted at
      `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py:825`, with `:776` guarding the retired
      singular ("whole library" must not reappear).
- [x] No new false-scope surface introduced or left inconsistent with the
      other three (tooltip, heading, launch prompt all agree) — all three go
      through the single composer `describeSDTScope()` (`bootstrap.js:616`),
      so the vocabulary cannot drift between them by construction.

## Scope

Follow-up to 0710, not a new design decision -- reuses `describeSDTScope()`
verbatim. Small.

